#!/bin/sh
# Normalization: the input has total weight 1, so the broadened spectrum integrates to 1. The log-Gaussian
# (Eq. 17a) and the -f' kernel both conserve weight; the trapezoidal estimate on the mesh must agree to 1e-3.
set -e
tools=$1; src=$2; dir=$3
perl "$dir/../make_input.pl" abin spec.abin spread
"$tools/abroaden" -M 10 -o spec.abin 1 0.3 1e-4 2 > abroaden.log
perl -e '
  my $weight;
  while (<>) { $weight = $1 if /^Estimated weight \(trapezoidal rule\)=(\S+)/; }
  die "no weight in the output\n" unless defined $weight;
  print "weight $weight\n";
  exit(abs($weight - 1) < 1e-3 ? 0 : 1);
' abroaden.log
